// Golden vectors, determinism, resume and the stage entry point of the
// climate stage (spec P1-03 sections 2, 3, 6 invariant 6, 7, 10.3 and 10.4;
// P1-00 sections 3, 5.1, 10.1, 14 X1 and X2; rule D10).
//
// The golden vectors in worldgen/tests/golden/p1-03-climate.txt were
// generated by worldgen/tests/reference/p1_climate_reference.py, the test
// writer's exact-integer reference written from the spec alone, with the
// input layers from the hydrology and elevation references. Each case's
// inputs are recomputed by the elevation and hydrology stages and checked
// first against the case's input items and the hydrology golden file, so an
// upstream change is reported as such and does not show as a climate
// failure. The items are then compared in step order, so a failure names
// the first step that diverges: the wind (C2), the surface, the
// temperature noise and T (the test's own C3), the temperature layer, hs
// (seam climate_box_mean), q and p (seam climate_sweep), the rainfall noise
// and the rainfall layer, then the report values.
//
// P1-03 10.4's own golden values (layer hashes at N = 512 and 1024 recorded
// by the validation specialist after the implementation passes) are not
// these: these are the test writer's per-step vectors. The N >= 512 cases,
// when the file holds them, run in the suite "climate-slow".
//
// Slow checks are in the test suite "climate-slow", skipped by default:
//   worldgen-tests -ts=climate-slow --no-skip

#include <doctest/doctest.h>

#include <algorithm>
#include <cstdint>
